# Tailscale is deliberately NOT a cask. It is installed once by
# installer/tailscale.sh from the standalone macsys pkg and self-updates via
# Sparkle after that, so the cask adds no upgrades -- only risk. The
# tailscale-app cask's uninstall stanza is `pkgutil: com.tailscale.ipn.macsys`,
# which deletes every file the pkg laid down. Because a cask upgrade is
# uninstall-then-install, any greedy upgrade (`brew cu`, `brew upgrade
# --greedy`) discards the node key, tailscaled re-authenticates from scratch,
# and the tailnet mints a *new* machine -- the old hostname is still taken, so
# the device comes back as `<host>-1`, `-2`, `-3`. Managing it in one place
# keeps the machine's tailnet identity stable.
